.TH TRACEROUTE 1 "2026-05-22" "hako" "hako utilities"
.SH NAME
traceroute \- print the route packets take to a network host
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B traceroute
.RI [@ nameserver ]
.I host
.RB [ \-m
.IR max_hops ]
.RB [ \-q
.IR nprobes ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B traceroute
discovers the sequence of routers between the local host and
.IR host
by sending ICMP echo-request packets with increasing TTL values.
Each router that discards a packet because its TTL expired returns an
ICMP Time Exceeded message; the source address of that message identifies
the hop.
When the destination itself replies with an ICMP Echo Reply the trace
is complete.
.PP
.I host
may be an IPv4 address or a hostname.
If a hostname is given it is resolved to an IPv4 address using DNS before
the first probe is sent.
The default nameserver is
.B 8.8.8.8
(Google Public DNS); an alternate resolver can be specified by prefixing
.BI @ address
(an IPv4 address) to the argument list.
.PP
For each TTL,
.I nprobes
(default 3) packets are sent.
The output line for that hop shows the replying router's address followed
by the round-trip time of each probe, or
.B *
for a probe that timed out (3 seconds per probe).
If all probes at a given TTL time out the address field is also shown as
.BR * .
.PP
.B traceroute
requires the ability to open a raw ICMP socket.
On Linux this typically requires
.BR CAP_NET_RAW ,
so the binary may need to be run as root or have the capability granted.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI "\-m " max_hops
Stop after
.I max_hops
hops.
Default:
.BR 30 .
.TP
.BI "\-q " nprobes
Send
.I nprobes
packets per TTL.
Default:
.BR 3 .
.SH OUTPUT FORMAT
.EX
traceroute to example.com (93.184.216.34), 30 hops max
 1  192.168.1.1  1.234 ms  1.456 ms  1.789 ms
 2  * * *
 3  10.0.0.1  5.123 ms  5.456 ms  5.789 ms
30  93.184.216.34  45.678 ms  45.890 ms  46.012 ms
.EE
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B "traceroute example.com"
Trace to
.B example.com
using the default settings.
.TP
.B "traceroute -m 15 -q 1 example.com"
Trace with a 15-hop limit and one probe per hop.
.TP
.B "traceroute @1.1.1.1 example.com"
Trace using Cloudflare's resolver for hostname lookup.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Trace completed (destination reached or max hops exhausted).
.TP
.B 1
Missing or invalid arguments, DNS resolution failure, or failure to
open a raw ICMP socket (often a permissions error).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR traceroute (8),
.BR ping (1),
.BR hako (1)
